<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=200" title="View the profile of Eelyen">Eelyen</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								The Overmind<br />
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 180<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.fotguild.com/images/avatars/eelavatar.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								The Overmind<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=200"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.fotguild.com" title="Fires of Time Guild" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1360.msg13405#msg13405"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1360.msg13405#msg13405">It's been 6 years of Everquest now.  I need help, your help.</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> December 26, 2004, 09:05:33 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							For the majority of that 6 years of Everquest, I have played on Rodcet Nife.  I started in Phase 4 beta back in January of 99, then played on Veeshan when Everquest went live.  Finally switching to Rodcet Nife and starting anew when the server opened on April 27th, 1999.  It&#039;s been a long 6 years.<br /><br />We all have memories, of good times and bad times.  Some people who visit board are very new to the game, some are very old to the game, and some are in between. But you all who visit this board are a major part of what this game has ment to me, what this game has meant to me, and what this game has done to me.<br /><br />For those who may ask, what happened to me.  Yes, I still play, just not on rodcet.  I&#039;ve be elsewhere since I stepped down.  Ironically, atm, I&#039;m in the same guild as Rogosh.  As sillk put it, someone up there has a sense of humor.  But that doesn&#039;t matter.<br /><br />I&#039;ve been wanting to make a <b>Flash</b> movie about Everquest and my time in the game for some time now.  Partly inspired by the movies of <a href="http://www.guildmirage.com" target="_blank">http://www.guildmirage.com</a>.  Partly inspired by the desires to show my history and what everquest has been to me.  <br /><br />But regardless of all that, I can make a movie, I can program, and I can be creative in how i do that.  I&#039;m not an artist, nor am I the most musical adept person out there.  <br /><br />I&#039;m not an expert at Flash either.  I&#039;ve always been a programmer.  I&#039;ve been very creative at what i&#039;ve focused on.  Logic.  Programming is easy when you are good at logic.  Flash is no exception.  It&#039;s really easy to do.  But being really creative in the process is hard.  I can make a flash movie.  But I need assistance.<br /><br />Which is why I come to yall today.  You as in Rodcet Nife, there are many talented people out there.  I have a few things I would ask your assistance of.  And please note, I&#039;m not a grammer major either... I just write code, so I ask as best I Can.<br /><br />1.  A Song to put the flash movie too.  You can&#039;t have a good movie without the music to back it.  The emotion behind the entire thing.  I&#039;ve spent countless hours listening to the music available too me.  I&#039;ve narrowed down a few songs I would use with what I&#039;ve got.  But the truth is, I&#039;ve never been big into music.  There is so much more talent out there and so many more people who know whats there.  <br /><br />I need a song.  I need <b>2 songs actually</b>.   The feelings I&#039;m going to ask for can be seperated among these songs.  Or together, but please try to focus on songs that convey these feelings.  I love songs with a beat, but the feelings for this flash movie are more important.   Try to convey the feeling of the song with Everquest...it doesn&#039;t have to be a 100% match..just something along the lines.  People can make the cooralation (sp is off I know).<br /><br />One of the songs should contain some feeling about love towards the game.  What has been lost or found.  What is happenign.  Or a sorrow about the past and/or a inspiration of some sorts about the future.  Basically what I&#039;m saying is I&#039;ve been through alot in the game.  Mainly with raiding guilds. It&#039;s always been about obtaining the best...being the best..and focusing and achieving the best.  It&#039;s been about fighting hard battles, sometimes hopeless battles, and sometimes about just fighting the battle of motivation.  Being in the high end is alot about motivation.  And a good song would show the pain and success of this fight.<br /><br />The other song would show more of a family side of everquest.  Everyone&#039;s side.  <b>WE</b> all meet people in this game.  Whether they effect us in good or bad ways, they are apart of us.  And this includes you (Grem and Karadana, who I despise the most, yet love ya so much as part of my history) whoever you may bet.  You are all part of the history of everquest.  The grouping times, the raiding times, the solo times, and the dying times.  The tradeskill times, the new n00b times, and the annoyed senior times.   This song should just give a general sorrow, happiness, or goodbye, type of theme.  A looking back type of memory song.  <br /><br />I would appreicate lots of submissions.  Give me the title of the song, if I don&#039;t have it, I&#039;ll go and listen to it as best I Can at a music store.  If you are fairly positive I can&#039;t find it at a music store (as if it&#039;s some sort of local band or foreign national band then just email me at my email at the bottom of this post, and I&#039;ll give you contact info).<br /><br /><b>Also</b>, I could use some extra screenshots for the flash movie.  It will not be Guild Mirage quality.  But I will do my best.  As Rodcet Nife has been a Huge part of my gaming experience, I feel the people of RN the opportunity to be a part of this movie.  While I want to convey a bit of my story in a rough fashion, I feel that the screenshots of others will help convery that.  And convey the family of Rodcet Nife.<br /><br />If you want to submit screenshots thats fine and I willing accept them.    Posting them on this forum is fine.  Although if you wish to email me, just let me know and I&#039;ll give you the info.<br /><br />Please...for screenshots, I want to have little to no UI in the movie as possible.  So please pick screenshots that allow me to covey the image without the clutterness of a UI in the screen.  Even if I have to cut it out, make sure the main focus of the screenshot is in the image, not the UI.  Text screenshots are not going in this movie.<br /><br />I appreciate the help.   This is going to be done in my freetime, but something I really want to see done.  The songs are my biggest blockade.  Once I have those nailed down...putting the images to the music are alot easier.    <br /><br />Thanks for reading.<br /><br />PS. Please ignore all spelling and grammer errors.....I am a programmer....not an english major for sure!!&#039;<br /><br /><br /><b>EDIT</b>: If in all doubt, please watch all guild mirage movies before submitting suggestiongs.  For screenshots, anyone can participate and submit. And I will try to add them to the movie.  But the song is very important.  So if you watch the guild mirage movies.   And see what I&#039;m talking about.   I will be considering very hard about the song.  I&#039;m not a song expert.  So I know someone will find a better song out there then I could.<br /><br />I will give credit for the song suggestion and all screenshots.<br /><br />If with enough screenshots from across the server.   It will probably become Rodcet Nife&#039;s Memory Album, instead of just whatever I decide to call it from my screenshots.<br /><br /><b>Edit2</b>: To Anyone who submits screenshots.  I will do my absolute best to include them in the movie.  The more, the better is what i say to you.  <br /><br /><b>Screenshots</b>: Send them too <a href="mailto:screenshots@eelyen.com">screenshots@eelyen.com</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: December 26, 2004, 11:09:59 am by Eelyen</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Sage Eelyen of the Nexus<br />Overmind of Fires of Time<br />Proud Member of the &lt;Hasbeens&gt;
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
